(The Bank of England, which is managed by a Governor, Sub-Governor, and) Tj T*
(twenty-four Directors, was incorporated in 1694 at the suggestion of a) Tj T*
(Scotsman, William Paterson, a man of roving disposition, whose Darien) Tj T*
(expedition proved a miserable fiasco, cost Scotland some г400,000, and) Tj T*
(shattered the health of Paterson, who died in London at the beginning) Tj T*
(of 1719, if not in poverty at least stripped of nearly all his fortune.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Schemes relating to the Isthmus of Darien \(or Panama\), that narrow) Tj T*
(little strip of land which unites the two Americas, have proved) Tj T*
(fruitful in disaster. France's great canal venture, we all remember,) Tj T*
(resulted in huge loss and grave scandal; and Paterson lived to bitterly) Tj T*
(regret his colonisation scheme, devoutly wishing that he had pinned) Tj T*
(his faith to his finance company, the Bank of England, for a finance) Tj T*
(company it then was in every sense of the word.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Little is known of William Paterson's early career, the various) Tj T*
(accounts relating thereto being meagre and conflicting, his enemies) Tj T*
(describing him as a mere adventurer, and his friends declaring that) Tj T*
(he was actuated by the worthiest of motives. However, when it is) Tj T*
(remembered that his second great venture \(the Darien scheme\) involved) Tj T*
(thousands in ruin, it is evident that had the man been a saint he would) Tj T*
(not have lacked detractors, and though his public utterances sound) Tj T*
(quaintly pious to the modern ear, it seems probable that he was only an) Tj T*
(enterprising merchant, whose morality was neither better nor worse than) Tj T*
(that of the times in which he lived.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The son of a Scotch farmer, Paterson left home at an early age, and,) Tj T*
(after settling for a short time in the West of England, set sail for) Tj T*
(the West Indies, returning to Europe about 1686 with the Darien scheme) Tj T*
(in his brain. Receiving but scant encouragement in England, despite the) Tj T*
(fact that his bank had been successfully floated, he concentrated his) Tj T*
(energies upon Scotland, where his scheme fired the public imagination,) Tj T*
(almost every Scotsman with a few pounds to invest eagerly taking the) Tj T*
(money to the company, convinced that Panama was the natural commercial) Tj T*
ET
