("Glorious Revolution," the "Divine right" of kings became a mere theory) Tj T*
(in this country, and the power of the Crown was made subservient to the) Tj T*
(will of the people. In short, the rule of Parliament began. The trade) Tj T*
(of the country gradually expanded, and with it the influence of the) Tj T*
(Bank.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(In order that we may thoroughly grasp the position previously occupied) Tj T*
(by the Bank of England, and the influence given to it by its connection) Tj T*
(with the Government, it will be better, before briefly discussing the) Tj T*
(Act of 1844, to revert to the days when the sway of the Bank of England) Tj T*
(was absolute.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(In 1708, we know, the Bank was granted the monopoly of joint stock) Tj T*
(banking in England, and, further, it was made illegal for any private) Tj T*
(firm, whose partners were more than six in number, to conduct the) Tj T*
(business of a banker. This restriction was not removed until 1857, when) Tj T*
(the partners in a private bank might consist of ten, and it will be) Tj T*
(seen from the following facts that this limitation was harmful to the) Tj T*
(best interests of the country.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(One result of this hard-and-fast enactment was the encouragement of) Tj T*
(small private banks in every county of England; but the fact that the) Tj T*
(number of their partners was limited to six effectually checked their) Tj T*
(expansion, and finally brought hundreds of them to the ground; for) Tj T*
(they could not strengthen themselves, and add to their resources, by) Tj T*
(amalgamation as is now possible.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(As the population of the country increased, the position of the private) Tj T*
